thought that blockchain

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.446
was all about cryptocurrencies.

00:04:43.446 --> 00:04:45.570
And actually, some of you
may be forgiven for still

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.280
feeling that way today.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.710
But the reality
is the blockchain

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.380
is a lot bigger than
cryptocurrencies.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.080
And the applications
go far and wide.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.490
So here, three and
a half or so years

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.150
later, is the vision of
our company, Digital Asset.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:07.150
Simply put, we believe
that blockchain offers

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.960
the opportunity to unleash
the kind of furiously-paced

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.770
innovation that the tech
industry has become accustomed

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.620
to over the past
10 years, and yet,

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.400
which has been notably absent
from financial services

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.740
and other giant
enterprise sectors--

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.340
from health care to
govtech and beyond.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.190
It will revolutionize
the processing

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:34.660
of every asset, every
transaction, every workflow,

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.750
across and within every
business and different companies

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.900
in the world.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.230
It's not a small vision.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.410
Now, to understand this, just
with any great technology

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.620
solution, you need to understand
what is the problem that

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.490
is being solved.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.270
15 years ago, if
you had predicted

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:59.710
that we would see the
advent of self-driving cars

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:03.250
more quickly than we
would discover the ability

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.040
to sell an equity and
get your cash for that

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:09.400
in less than two days,
or that even you'd

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.370
have the simple privilege
of walking from one doctor's

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:16.180
office to the next and
expecting your medical records

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.580
and identity to
travel with you, you

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.860
would have been declared insane.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:25.990
But the reality is that we got
the self-driving car first.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.450
How on Earth could
that be the case?

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.770
Well, the answer lies in
something as banal and mundane

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.900
as data architecture.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.540
It turns out that
enterprise infrastructure,

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.480
from financial services
to health and beyond,

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:45.520
has been stymied by what
we call silo-ization.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.870
Why?

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.960
Because businesses can't
securely trust, or could not

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:55.600
until now, their ability
to share and process data

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.970
without compromising
their responsibility

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:03.740
for their books and records and
confidentiality and privacy.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:08.290
Now, what silos lead to
is unnecessary duplication

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:15.670
of records, error-prone
updates, asymmetric information,

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.250
expensive and
time-consuming breaks--

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.500
and literally, in
financial services

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.620
alone, tens of billions
of dollars a year

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:27.880
in a completely zero-value-added
effort of reconciling-- that

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.010
means ticking and
tying records that

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.130
are different that should,
in fact, be the same simply

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:36.100
because they didn't share
a common or golden source

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.190
of record.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.860
It was my exposure
over almost 30 years,

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.070
in the bowels of the
financial services industry,

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.710
to the understanding
of the sheer scale

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:50.910
of the cost, the waste, the
inefficiency, and ultimately

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:54.360
the risk associated
with this that

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:57.300
led me to believe
all-in in blockchain

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.830
and to move to Digital Asset.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.320
Blockchain, or as it has
become known as DLT--

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:10.940
Distributed Ledger Technology--
will change all of this.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:16.520
Simply put, it's a new form of
secure database architecture

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:19.880
that offers businesses,
enterprise, for the first time

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:25.850
certainty of shared,
real-time identical records,

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:30.620
synchronized processing,
programmable, automatable

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:35.570
assets and associated workflows,
without loss of privacy

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:39.230
or confidentiality,
and without continuing

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:42.380
to have responsibility for being
able to independently validate

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.770
your own books and records.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.490
Just as the internet
unleashed and liberated

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:52.610
the free flow of
information 20 years ago

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:55.310
and changed
everything, blockchain

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.190
is going to liberate
the processing of value,

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.610
saving hundreds of billions
of dollars of cost,

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.430
and unleashing innovation.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.710
To hear more about
how this will happen,

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.050
I'll introduce you to
two of my colleagues--

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.900
our CTO, Shaul Kfir,
and our chief marketing

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:15.210
officer, Dan O'Prey.

